plugin-hostd (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pins are learned on first use: the first time a plugin is added its pin
    is recorded in a pin store, and a later change of the plugin or its
    layout is announced instead of passing silently.
  * pin_file names the pin store; saves are fsync'd so a crash never loses a
    pin, and a corrupt or overlong store line is refused rather than trusted.
  * One format table holds a row per plugin format: the pins and the
    supervisor read the row, so a new format needs no changes elsewhere, and
    the protocol names capabilities instead of formats.
  * The packages require omx-clap-host-tests as a floor only, no ceiling.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

